The `einsum` path is slower because it appears to do its own layout work. I’m going to try a more targeted layout change: fuse sigmoid/mask with a transpose-oriented Triton post kernel that writes `left/right` directly as contiguous rows for each hidden channel, avoiding the two explicit permute copies while keeping `out_gate` in the layout the final norm expects.
